{#
    The IdP's front page. `/simplesaml/` redirects here, and so does a sign-out
    of the IdP itself (core/logout without a ReturnTo). Stock, it describes the
    SimpleSAMLphp software and drops out of the UBC look. Someone can arrive
    here without ever having signed in, so it must not tell them they are
    "signed out": it says what this service is, how to sign in, and how to
    switch test account.
#}
{% set pagetitle = 'UBC test identity provider' %}
{% extends "@core/_layout.twig" %}

{% block content %}
<div class="container">
    <div class="row-fluid">
        <div class="span12">
            <h1>UBC test identity provider</h1>
            <p>
                This is a SimpleSAMLphp identity provider for local development. It stands in
                for CWL so that an application can be built and tested against a CWL-shaped
                sign-in. It knows only test accounts, and a real CWL password should never be
                typed into it.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row-fluid">
        <div class="span8">
            <div class="well">
                <h4>Signing in</h4>
                <p>Start from your application: it sends you here to sign in, and back again.</p>
                <h4>Signing in as a different test account</h4>
                <p>
                    Signing out of an application does not always end your session with this
                    identity provider, and while that session lasts, the next sign-in skips the
                    password and returns the same account. To choose another account,
                    <a href="{{ moduleURL('core/logout/example-userpass') }}">end your session with this identity provider</a>
                    first, then sign in from your application again.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
